## What exists today

| Piece | Status |
| --- | --- |
| `demote_to_parameter`: sever a quantity's conditional, keep its identity | built |
| `stacked_tangent`, `JointNormal`, `add_joint_factor`: a joint over existing quantities | built |
| `remove_closure` and mark-and-sweep `cleanup` | built |
| `marginalize_out`, `joint_normal_from`: the Schur complement as a whitening, and its factor | built |
| An estimator to solve each window | missing (see [the pose example](../example-pose-estimation/#what-exists-today)) |

Two things nothing can check for you:

- a hand-built `JointNormal`'s whitening must be expressed in the same block order as its ids
  (`joint_normal_from` keeps it by construction);
- a joint factor binds no `LOCATION` or `WHITENING`, so `GaussianBlock` does not see it.

See [Status and roadmap](../../reference/status/).
